# Frontend Entity Display Constitution

Human-readable entity columns, correct filters, and layout width matching page intent are
mandatory for catalog and cross-reference surfaces.

## Non-negotiables

- Never show raw UUID or internal id as the primary visible value in a user-facing table column or summary field.
- Entity primary labels link to detail routes when the session has read access; plain text when not.
- Use `EntityLinkCell` for entity columns — do not hand-roll link + truncate logic per view.
- Filters: enum → select; entity reference → async `AppSearchSelect`; free-text only when the API supports substring search on that field.
- Table-heavy catalog pages: `AppPageLayout layoutVariant="fluid"`. Forms/detail/workspace: `layoutVariant="contained"` (1440px).
- Prefer `CatalogFilterToolbar` for catalog filter rows; extend via shared types, not page-local filter bars.

